<!--
    File:     prop_vsc_12x6.xml
    Author:   Cheon
    Date:     2026-03-26
    Description: VSC 12×6 propeller model for Goshawk 10S

    Propeller Specifications:
    - Model: VSC 12×6
    - Diameter: 12 inches (0.5334 meters)
    - Pitch: 6 inches (0.1524 meters)
    - Pitch Ratio: 0.5 (6/12)
    - Type: Fixed pitch, multirotor propeller
    - Blades: 2 (typical for this size)

    Motor: T-motor AT3520 550KV
    - Max thrust: 2.6920 kg (5.9348441 lbs) per motor @ 100% throttle
    - Max power: 1100 W
    - Max RPM: ~13860 RPM (at 6S/25.2V)

    Performance Characteristics:
    - Low pitch ratio (0.5) optimized for high static thrust
    - Suitable for VTOL/hover operations
    - Good efficiency at low advance ratios

    Notes:
    - Thrust and power coefficients are estimated based on typical
      multirotor propeller characteristics
    - For precise modeling, measured propeller data is recommended
    - Static thrust matches motor specifications (~11.1 kg per motor)
-->

<propeller name="prop_vsc_12x6">
    <!-- Propeller inertia (estimated for 12" carbon fiber propeller) -->
    <ixx> 0.0002 </ixx> <!-- slug-ft^2 -->

    <!-- Physical dimensions -->
    <diameter unit="IN"> 12 </diameter>
    <numblades> 2 </numblades>
    <gearratio> 1.0 </gearratio> <!-- Direct drive, no gearbox -->

    <!-- Pitch characteristics -->
    <minpitch> 6 </minpitch> <!-- Fixed pitch propeller -->
    <maxpitch> 6 </maxpitch>

    <!-- RPM limits -->
    <minrpm> 0 </minrpm>

    <!-- Conservative limit for electric motor -->
    <!-- <maxrpm> 10487 </maxrpm>  -->
    
    <!-- Maximum RPM for electric motor -->
    <maxrpm> 13860 </maxrpm> 

    <!--
    Thrust Coefficient Table: C_T vs Advance Ratio (J)

    Advance Ratio: J = V / (n * D)
    where:
      V = velocity (ft/s)
      n = RPM / 60 (revolutions per second)
      D = diameter (ft)

    For low pitch ratio propellers (0.335):
    - High static thrust (J=0)
    - Efficiency peaks at low advance ratios
    - Quick thrust dropoff at higher speeds

    Thrust calculation: T = C_T * ρ * n² * D⁴
    where ρ = air density (slugs/ft³)

    Target static thrust: ~11.1 kg = 24.5 lbs = 109 N
    At max RPM (6500): C_T ≈ 0.12 for this propeller
    -->
    <table name="C_THRUST" type="internal">
        <tableData>
		0.00	0.09292
        0.05	0.08882
        0.10	0.08416
        0.15	0.07895
        0.20	0.07319
        0.25	0.06688
